// #disable / #enable. The disable set is keyed by rule NUMBER (1-based, one per
// OP_RULE in instruction order) but checked against the rule's FIRST
// instruction, which is what both the sequential loop and csp_react enter
// csp_eval_rule with -- so one test covers both dispatch paths, and this file
// runs in BOTH modes to prove they agree.
//
// Rules 1 and 2 are seeded <- bindings: without the seed neither would ever
// fire (Y never changes), so a rule that runs at all is visible as a non-zero
// result. Rule 3 is disabled and then re-enabled, so it must still run.
#variable Y integer = 7
#variable X integer = 0
#variable Z integer = 0
#variable W integer = 0

X <- Y + 1
Z <- Y + 2
W <- Y + 3

#disable 2-3
#enable 3
